      <node id="113329333853512625" label="aws, Black Walnuts, and a smattering of other plants. Once we got power and running water back to take showers earlier this week (more than 2 weeks without) we started to get into the muck and cleaning garbage out. This is after we've pulled out at least 8 contractor bags out. Plastic, dryer sheets, clothing, tires, sheets of metal and vinyl from trailers, wood, part of a boat, wiring, more plastic, more dryer sheets, yet more plastic wrapped with dryer sheets and dead leaves. I have become radicalized against dryer sheets. The only things doing well down here right now are all invasive species. The good news is wildlife ate all the rotting maggot-filled fish that had flooded out of the nearby fish farm. Downstream of here a nearby town gets their water. #appalachia #hurricanehelene #northcarolina#appalachiaappalachia#hurricanehelenehurricanehelene#northcarolinanorthcarolina">
        <attvalues>
