          <attvalue for="5" value="root" />
          <attvalue for="6" value="https://tech.lgbt/@athos/113326132080603065" />
          <attvalue for="7" value="1.0" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113325830482240180" label="n a disaster and I'm like.. how did y'all forget already that fuel was completely unavailable for days even once roads were vaguely passable??? And then it was being rationed out and they would only accept cash?? A little PV solar system means you're directly generating power from the sun you don't need to rely on grids or supply lines. For some reason some folks are convinced that solar is for the bourgeoisie or something. Something they don't like to talk about - at ALL - is how much fuel their generators take. And the fuel doesn't keep indefinitely. All systems have points of failure but I am shocked by the reluctance for more people who claim some manner of self reliance to not embrace solar more. #hurricanehelene #disasterpreparedness #solar#hurricanehelenehurricanehelene#disasterpreparednessdisasterpreparedness#solarsolar">
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="2024-10-18 01:28:59+00:00" />
          <attvalue for="1" value="planty@sunbeam.city" />
          <attvalue for="2" value="4" />
