      <node id="113225085745735549" label=" network is? The work we’ve done over the past several years has made it possible for to relatively easily be found and connect with folks who are bringing supplies from afar — en route from New Orleans, Michigan and Vermont at this moment, among other places!With the funds we’ve collected so far we were able to help buy the needed materials for someone who has a mobile kitchen to get the supplies she needs and head from Virginia to the impacted zone.At one point in the day there was a moment of panic when the authorities said Bee Tree damn was close to imminent failure. Turns out it was just spilling over in a way it was designed to do. Whew!While roads are opening up and crews in our network made it to Asheville and Boone today, sadly there ares which are still completely cut off due to washed out roads. The images and stories coming from these places are heartbreaking. Below is an image from Hot Springs, NC we got by email today. Some folks in our network are trying to figure out how to equip themselves with portable water filtration devices which will fit in backpacks to try and reach some of these areas.&quot; #MutualAid #HurricaneHelene#MutualAidMutualAid#HurricaneHeleneHurricaneHelenehttps://www.patreon.com/posts/hurricane-helene-113043619https://www.patreon.com/posts/hurricane-helene-113043619https://www.patreon.com/posts/hurricane-helene-113043619">
