      <node id="113214744093770178" label="sy season for tropical cyclones and hurricanes from the dozen or more orgs that forecast the season back in June, the north Atlantic basin was uncannily quiet for the thick end of three months. (Ironically, it seems likely that the main reason for the quiet was changes in large-scale climate patterns caused by... global warming.) Anyway, following last week's devastation across the US SE from Hurricane Helene, the Atlantic certainly seems to have woken up with a vengeance now, and is making up for lost time... #hurricanehelene #hurricane #globalwarming #climate #storms#hurricanehelenehurricanehelene#hurricanehurricane#globalwarmingglobalwarming#climateclimate#stormsstorms">
