      <node id="113404524316443224" label="rolinaFrom NC Emergency Management on FB: ICYMI: Last week, Governor Roy Cooper issued an Executive Order focused on easing requirements and fee collections for North Carolinians related to the Division of Motor Vehicles (DMV) in counties impacted by Hurricane Helene. As a result of this Order, the DMV will suspend the collection of various application and late fees, suspend certain requirements for both residents and businesses, and extend certain licenses for mechanics and businesses. Read more at: https://governor.nc.gov/news/press-releases/2024/10/24/governor-cooper-issues-executive-order-ease-dmv-requirements-and-fee-collections-western-north.https://governor.nc.gov/news/press-releases/2024/10/24/governor-cooper-issues-executive-order-ease-dmv-requirements-and-fee-collections-western-northhttps://governor.nc.gov/news/press-releases/2024/10/24/governor-cooper-issues-executive-order-ease-dmv-requirements-and-fee-collections-western-north">
