      <node id="113367796086672824" label="hCarolinaFrom NC Emergency Management on FB: Attention Helene Responders: Please be aware that bear, small game, and deer (archery) are in season in Western North Carolina. A few ways you can stay safe: • Identify hunting areas near your mission. • Wear orange in hunting areas.• Never approach wildlife.• Secure food, garbage, and donations.• Be aware of rotting food in damaged homes or businesses – they may attract bears.• Drive slow and pay attention to bushes &amp; trees where wildlife may be hiding. To find designated hunting areas, visit https://www.ncwildlife.org/hunting/where-hunt-shoot/game-lands-maps or https://www.ncpaws.org/ncwrcmaps/gamelands.https://www.ncwildlife.org/hunting/where-hunt-shoot/game-lands-mapshttps://www.ncwildlife.org/hunting/where-hunt-shoot/game-lands-mapshttps://www.ncpaws.org/ncwrcmaps/gamelandshttps://www.ncpaws.org/ncwrcmaps/gamelands">
