      <node id="113278123093439841" label="hCarolinaFrom NC Emergency Management on FB: On Tuesday, October 8, Governor Roy Cooper traveled to Burnsville in Yancey County and Spruce Pine in Mitchell County and was joined by FEMA Federal Emergency Management Agency Administrator Deanne Criswell, Federal Highway Administration Acting Administrator Kristin White and other state and federal officials to assess storm damage, thank volunteers and speak with people impacted by Hurricane Helene. Read more on the latest #HeleneNC efforts at: https://bit.ly/3XXei7I.#HeleneNCHeleneNChttps://bit.ly/3XXei7Ihttps://bit.ly/3XXei7I">
        <attvalues>
