      <node id="113258298987307266" label="disposal are waived to some extent for a limited time in the areas named in disaster proclamations; this allows debris from burned or flooded homes that would normally have to be tested for toxicity and then taken to very expensive hazardous waste facilities to be taken directly to special dispoal areas at permitted landfills; your state may even open special disposal sites for this purpose; contrarily, if such disposal is being proposed near your property or in your watershed, be ready to fight any efforts to skip necessary environmental protections, either by local governments or private contractors; installing liners, clay caps, monitoring wells, and final cover that will support plants and wildlife is expensive, but much of the cost should be covered by the state or Feds; a good job might result in a useful recreation area—a bad job will give you a toxic mess that the perpetrators will walk away from. #helene@ai6yr@ai6yrai6yr#helenehelene">
