      <node id="113251562195213291" label="hCarolinaNorthCarolinaFrom NC Emergency Management on FB: North Carolina Emergency Management officials are cautioning the public about false Helene reports and misinformation being shared on social media. Misinformation, particularly online, has led to false news reports and rumors about coordinated response efforts. Dangerous conditions continue in some areas and false information could put people at risk. Read more on how you can help avoid the spread of rumors at: https://www.ncdps.gov/news/press-releases/2024/10/04/state-emergency-response-team-publishing-guide-highlighting-trusted-information-sources.  #HeleneNC #WNCStrong.https://www.ncdps.gov/news/press-releases/2024/10/04/state-emergency-response-team-publishing-guide-highlighting-trusted-information-sourceshttps://www.ncdps.gov/news/press-releases/2024/10/04/state-emergency-response-team-publishing-guide-highlighting-trusted-information-sources#HeleneNCHeleneNC#WNCStrongWNCStrong">
