      <node id="113248780285369840" label="Taiwan and she told us how things were going with the island-wide shutdown for #Typhoon #Krathon. Another friend gave us an update on her sister who lives in a small town outside of #Asheville. She has running water so she built a shower in the front yard for her neighbors. I said I’ve been worried since #Helene about the people I met who live at Mountain Gardens, a sort of sanctuary for rare medicinal herbs on steep terrain at the top of a dirt road up under Mount Mitchell. Another work friend (in #Portland so we’ve been through fire seasons and heat domes together remotely) dug through platforms I’m not on and found some posts from them. One was a video: sheets of brown water washing their gardens down the hill. A few hours later I was on a call with people in #Phoenix. I think they said it was 113 there at the time. We talked for a while about what it’s like to live in a city that hot. One of them said they had moved there from New Orleans after #Katrina. “I think I like to be in places where I can see it really happening.” At the end of the day I was writing something and I had to check how to spell the name of a river. It’s in a far away city I won’t ever visit because I think I’m done flying. I pulled up a map and there was a warning note on it saying the area was under travel restrictions. That river was flooding too. #TyphoonTyphoon#KrathonKrathon#AshevilleAsheville#HeleneHelene#PortlandPortland#PhoenixPhoenix#KatrinaKatrina#ClimateDiary#ClimateDiaryClimateDiary">
        <attvalues>
