      <node id="113238770992893536" label="lobal semiconductor industry.Spuce Pine, NC, mines 70% of ultra pure quartz needed to make CPUs and GPUs.Damage to town and mine is unknown, but likely serious, and that may lead to major global CPU/GPU shortages.We're in a bind; digital supply chains are fragile and dependent on a stable climate. But digital technologies are pulling us in the opposite direction.#ai #climate #helene. https://www.wired.com/story/hurricane-helene-shockwaves-semiconductor-industry-microchips-spruce-pine-north-carolina-sand-high-quality-quartz/#intcid=_wired-verso-hp-trending_a783839d-aaca-4e64-90db-2e71866ef97f_popular4-1#aiai#climateclimate#helenehelenehttps://www.wired.com/story/hurricane-helene-shockwaves-semiconductor-industry-microchips-spruce-pine-north-carolina-sand-high-quality-quartz/#intcid=_wired-verso-hp-trending_a783839d-aaca-4e64-90db-2e71866ef97f_popular4-1https://www.wired.com/story/hurricane-helene-shockwaves-semiconductor-industry-microchips-spruce-pine-north-carolina-sand-high-quality-quartz/#intcid=_wired-verso-hp-trending_a783839d-aaca-4e64-90db-2e71866ef97f_popular4-1">
