      <node id="113237427505943342" label="m North Carolina’s Weather Authority 5:47 am edt: A new one is ahead across the state; regardless of how bad the last few days have been, we can come together and make it better. Happy Wednesday, North Carolina! Looking over the morning data, we have a trough pulling away and a ridge moving in. We will have areas of fog this morning; it'll be slow to burn off, so expect partly sunny skies by late in the day. Highs today will be in the 70s and low 80s for most areas, and it will be cooler where clouds start around longer. A few isolated showers/drizzle are possible but nothing much. It'll be a quiet next few days of weather…-Ethan">
