      <node id="113227660218138949" label="naNorthCarolina#WataugaCountyWataugaCountyFrom Town of Boone, North Carolina 9/29/24:Watauga County, Town of Boone, Appalachian SU and partners are collaborating to keep our community informed... Continue to check this post for updates.To keep our 911 call center open for emergency calls, please use the following numbers:- (828) 268-6200 Boone Town Hall: 7 a.m. to 7 p.m., with hours subject to change.- (828) 263-4178 Appalachian Medical Reserve Corps Non-Emergency Call Center (for non-urgent inquiries and reports related to storm impacts): 8 a.m. to 8 p.m., and if the line is busy or it’s after hours, leave a message.- (828) 262-2000 Appalachian SU Main Line: 8 a.m. to 5 p.m.">
