      <node id="113222758619771533" label="ng up the cars and filling the bathtub and jugs with water. They have plenty of food and a gas stove. Mom is cooking up the pork chops that thawed in the freezer. They got a little bit of water on the downhill edge of basement floor, but that is IT for damage, which is fricking amazing. The worst of it for them is the inconvenience of not bathing and the cabin fever. Dad apparently has already read all of the books and thinks he is going to the library tomorrow to get new ones. (Ooooooo kay, Dad.) Dad has a hard time sitting still. He has already been out in the truck, and the main road is clear with little damage. Abandoned vehicles were sitting in the road. Long lines at the pumps, but there is no electricity. So, there is no way to get gas at the moment. Mom and the neighbors sure wish he wouldn’t wander but he can’t not. They are leaving the admonishments to me. I gave him a list of towns that have been washed away or otherwise decimated and that we won’t know the full death toll for a while and that he is incredibly lucky and it is best that he conserve resources and stays where he is. In typical Dad fashion he claimed he doesn’t need people treating him like he is an old man and that he will outlive them all. 🙄 I joked with Mom that she probably agreed to go driving with him so that she’d know where to find his body. #Helene #NCwx#HeleneHelene#NCwxNCwx">
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="2024-09-29 20:36:30+00:00" />
          <attvalue for="1" value="alysonsee@sunny.garden" />
