      <node id="113205575898652593" label="time. They get worse near shore as the seafloor rises, pushing water up. The worst scenario is when you have a bottleneck, much like the Big Bend coast of Florida, and especially in inlets that become narrower. The water gets pushed into a smaller space and had nowhere to go but up.  #Hurricane #Helene could produce storm surge up to 20 feet tall,  an “unsurvivable scenario,” said NHC director Michael Brennan.#HurricaneHurricane#HeleneHelene">
