      <node id="113205390200681106" label=". You've heard that the storm surge from #Hurricane #Helene may reach 20' (6 m) in places. But that's just the baseline, like a tide; the waves are on TOP of that. And the waves there tonight will be &quot;13 to 18 feet, occasionally to 23 feet&quot; (4 to 5.5 m, occ. to 7 m).#HurricaneHurricane#HeleneHelene20' plus 23' equals 43' (13m).Cedar Key is mostly 10' (3m) above sea level. The other keys &quot;barely make it to 20 feet [6 m] above the waves.&quot; The highest point on Florida's *entire Gulf Coast* is a ridgeline only 52' high (16 m).The highest point on the Florida Gulf Coast (a ridgeline on Cedar Key) is only nine feet higher than the predicted combo of storm surge + biggest waves.If you're still there and can get out, please get out.">
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="2024-09-26 18:59:27+00:00" />
          <attvalue for="1" value="msbellows@c.im" />
          <attvalue for="2" value="6" />
