      <node id="113203906893284166" label="ce to the north of the storm anyway, you can see from the wind map how the storm is pulling moisture in from that system as well as moist air up from the Caribbean. And all that while sitting over record warm water with no shear to bother it. This kind of interaction is called the Fujiwhara effect when both systems are cyclonic, but this is sort of a similar amplifying effect. https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fujiwhara_effect#helenehttps://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fujiwhara_effecthttps://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fujiwhara_effect#helenehelene">
