      <node id="113195016301710010" label="ut 2 hours ago. Folks tend to assume a more linear track means higher predictability. The problem with that is error bars in potential storm acceleration complicating tidal synchrony / storm surge forecasts on approach. The good news is off peak lunar tides. The bad news is potential storm radius (not in the update; speculative). Bit o lag here. Integration vs datahttps://www.youtube.com/live/fzd6plQiA1s?si=l5BYookcTBsh_5mZ#TropicalStormTropicalStorm#HeleneHelene#NHCNHC#MiamiMiamihttps://www.youtube.com/live/fzd6plQiA1s?si=l5BYookcTBsh_5mZhttps://www.youtube.com/live/fzd6plQiA1s?si=l5BYookcTBsh_5mZ">
