      <node id="113395967141446363" label="/153497/ghost-forests-creep-into-north-carolinahttps://earthobservatory.nasa.gov/images/153497/ghost-forests-creep-into-north-carolinahttps://earthobservatory.nasa.gov/images/153497/ghost-forests-creep-into-north-carolina&quot;Increasingly, #NorthCarolina’s bald cypress and other coastal #forests have a more ghoulish appearance. Instead of healthy green #trees, large swaths of cypress and pine forests in the area have died, shed their bark, and become pale, leafless snags that line the waterways like gravestones. In the period before winds topple the snags over and shrubs cover them up, researchers call the eerie ecosystems #GhostForests.&quot;#NorthCarolinaNorthCarolina#forestsforests#treestrees#GhostForestsGhostForests">
