      <node id="113333665755517871" label="rolina’s Weather Authority on FB: It's a new day across the state, and the weather will be A+ for the most part. Happy SAT, NC! It is chilly this morning, but high pressure will firmly control our weather, and it will warm up nicely. I expect mostly sunny skies, with highs in the 60s and 70s for most areas. It'll be a great fall day. King tides are expected along the coast; coastal flooding is possible for parts of the coast and likely for the Outer Banks today. The best chance for coastal flooding will be at 9AM around high tide in the common areas along the Outer Banks and the rest of the coast. Ocean overwash is possible. -Ethan">
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="2024-10-19 10:41:37+00:00" />
