      <node id="113271387915989331" label="lina’s Weather Authority on FB: Fall moves in, and a new day is ahead across the state. Happy Tuesday, North Carolina! Looking at the morning data, a cold front passed through overnight, and temps are down in most areas in the 50s and even 40s. I expect mostly sunny skies; high pressure will build into it, and it'll be a great day. Highs will be in the 70s for most areas, with some 60s to the west. It'll be a tranquil day, thanks to drier conditions. Temperatures will fall into the 40s and 50s tonight. Have a great day. -Ethan">
