      <node id="113267721265360164" label="lina’s Weather Authority on FB: FALL WEATHER COMING: Our first major fall cold front will slide through the state tonight; highs will drop into the 60s and 70s (a little warmer along the coast tomorrow) over the next few days through Friday. Lows will be in the 40s and 50s statewide, with some areas getting into the 30s in the higher elevations over the next few days. Please be aware of this for folks who still don't have power or housing in the mountains…Dry weather is expected tomorrow through Thursday statewide, with a couple of showers possible Friday along the coast. Otherwise, the weekend is looking dry statewide, too. -Ethan">
