      <node id="113254636121270563" label="new day across the state, and it'll be nice and quiet. Happy Saturday, North Carolina! I expect a rather tranquil day; looking at the morning data, the radar is quiet; there is some patchy fog out there but otherwise, nothing else is going on. We can expect partly to mostly sunny skies today as a trough slides south into SC/GA today. Highs today will be in the 70s and low 80s for most areas...can't completely rule out a stray popup shower or two late this afternoon and evening, but 98% of the state will be dry today. A few models try to bring some shower growth across Central NC, so I won't rule it out, especially with the day's heating. -Ethan">
