      <node id="113249685420951814" label="om North Carolina’s Weather Authority on FB: Radar Update: The radar is quiet right now, but a few scattered showers and even a thunderstorm will be possible this afternoon and evening. An isolated storm could bring some heavy rain along the mountains; this is just a heads-up for people who work in the mountains and live there. Usually, I would not be too concerned, but I don't want anyone to be caught off guard, especially with limited communications. Elsewhere across the state, only an isolated shower. This weekend still looks dry and sunny for most areas, with only an isolated shower and nothing much.   -Ethan">
