      <node id="113243064993079464" label="m North Carolina’s Weather Authority: It's a new day ahead across the state with rather tranquil weather conditions expected. Happy Thursday, North Carolina! Looking over the morning data, I see there is some fog out there; otherwise, it is quiet. High pressure at the surface will extend into our state from off the New England coast; it'll allow for a rather quiet day. I expect partly sunny skies with highs in the 70s and low 80s for most areas. While it should be a mostly quiet day, a couple of popup showers can't be ruled out, especially in the West. They'll not produce any heavy rainfall though…-Ethan">
