      <node id="113269777899441908" label="s dropped 20 mb of pressure. It is expected to intensify again, once it completes, but it will hit shear as it approaches Florida, lowering its intensity, but causing it to spread out, increasing the potential storm surge risk for many areas. It will be catastrophic, even if it is a high category 3 or low category 4 storm at landfall. Additionally, a lot of Florida hasn't finished draining from Helene. Storm surge is expected to be the greatest risk for many coastal communities.https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FUQxRiNQlzshttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FUQxRiNQlzshttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FUQxRiNQlzs#hurricane #Milton#hurricanehurricane#MiltonMilton">
