      <node id="113216242690103870" label="roject#ThailandThailand#MekongMekongCarolyn Cowan24 Sep 2024 Key points:-    Major flooding along Mekong tributaries in northern Thailand has heightened scrutiny of plans to build a major hydropower dam spanning the pivotal watercourse over the border in Laos.-    Experts say the Pak Beng Dam would worsen severe seasonal flooding by elevating water levels upstream into the stretch of the Mekong that flows through northern Thailand.-    In 2023, Thailand’s national electricity authority signed an agreement to purchase electricity from the controversial scheme, essentially greenlighting the next phase of development.-    This week, farmers, activists and policymakers met in the flood-prone province of Chiang Rai to discuss the potential cross-border impacts of the dam, with many speakers urging the Thai government and Thailand-based investors to reconsider their support of the scheme due to the risks of the dam exacerbating devastating floods.Read more:https://news.mongabay.com/2024/09/record-breaking-floods-in-northern-thailand-intensify-scrutiny-of-mekong-dam-project/https://news.mongabay.com/2024/09/record-breaking-floods-in-northern-thailand-intensify-scrutiny-of-mekong-dam-project/https://news.mongabay.com/2024/09/record-breaking-floods-in-northern-thailand-intensify-scrutiny-of-mekong-dam-project/#ExtremeWeather #ExtremeWx #Flooding #MekongDamProject #ClimateCrisis #ClimateCatastrophe#ExtremeWeatherExtremeWeather#ExtremeWxExtremeWx#FloodingFlooding#MekongDamProjectMekongDamProject#ClimateCrisisClimateCrisis#ClimateCatastropheClimateCatastrophe">
